ogsr-fidelityfx-fsr3 provides CMake targets:

    find_package(ogsr-fidelityfx-fsr3 CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE ogsr::ffx::fsr3upscaler ogsr::ffx::backend_dx11)   # or ogsr::ffx::backend_dx12
    # FSR3 frame generation (DX12): ogsr::ffx::fsr3 ogsr::ffx::frameinterpolation ogsr::ffx::opticalflow ogsr::ffx::backend_dx12

MSBuild (vcpkg manifest mode): define FFX_GCC (static FFX_API); #include <FidelityFX/host/ffx_fsr3.h>, <FidelityFX/host/backends/dx11/ffx_dx11.h>
or <FidelityFX/host/backends/dx12/ffx_dx12.h>; ffx_fsr3upscaler_x64.lib, ffx_fsr3_x64.lib, ffx_frameinterpolation_x64.lib,
ffx_opticalflow_x64.lib, ffx_backend_dx11_x64.lib and ffx_backend_dx12_x64.lib are auto-linked (the DX12 backend's shader blob lookups
have their own names, so both backends link into one exe). The DX12 backend calls CreateDXGIFactory2: an MSBuild consumer
links dxgi.lib itself (winmm / dwmapi come with the SDK's #pragma comment lines).
